{
  "raw": {
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204753": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Accounting (Tenure Track) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Accounting (Tenure Track) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Accounting (Tenure Track) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Accounting, Finance and Economics Locations: Mt Berry, GA Posted: Sep 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204753 Share Job Description: The Department of Accounting and Finance at Berry College invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting beginning August 2027. Rooted in Berry's mission of educating the head, heart, and hands, we seek a teacher-mentor-scholar committed to excellent teaching, meaningful scholarship, and preparing students for successful careers in accounting and related professions. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in federal taxation and an interest in helping students navigate a profession increasingly shaped by artificial intelligence and other emerging technologies. The AACSB -accredited Campbell School of Business offers a close-knit, collaborative environment with small classes, strong faculty-student mentoring, and a distinctive commitment to experiential learning through research, internships, LifeWorks (student work and professional development), and connections with employers and alumni. Faculty are encouraged to bring creativity to the classroom and to help students connect rigorous business education with practical experience and personal development. Teaching responsibilities include undergraduate and MBA accounting courses, with a primary need in federal taxation. The standard teaching load is 18 credit hours (typically six courses) per year. The successful candidate will maintain an active research agenda consistent with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) standards. Professional accounting credentials such as the CPA, CMA, or CIA, relevant professional experience, and experience integrating technology into accounting education are especially valued. Requirements: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. or DBA in Accounting or a closely related field, and candidates who are currently ABD should earn their doctoral degree by the date of employment. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interview or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values ; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on October 5 and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Xin Geng, at xgeng@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204209": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Biology (Tenure Track) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Biology (Tenure Track) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Biology (Tenure Track) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Biology Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204209 Share Job Description: The Biology Department at Berry College seeks a tenure-track assistant professor of biology to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate is expected to establish a strong teaching and research program that emphasizes molecular biology. Special consideration will be given to candidates with expertise in developmental biology and/or those who can utilize Berry's vast and biologically rich campus. This faculty member will offer courses and research opportunities that help students understand and explore their relationship with the natural world and gain hands-on professional growth and research experiences in molecular biology. The candidate will also serve as a liaison with Berry's Biochemistry program. Berry College's stunning 27,000-acre campus in a biologically rich ecoregion affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. The surrounding area extends the opportunities and includes forests, rivers, and other ecosystems that are home to many rare and endemic species. The biology department is known for innovative pedagogy, collaboration across disciplines, and mentorship of students from a wide range of backgrounds. The candidate should share our commitment to student engagement both inside and outside of the classroom, as well as our desire to promote opportunities for students from a wide range of backgrounds from underrepresented groups by participating in existing and developing new student outreach opportunities. Beyond the department, the successful candidate should also be an active participant in the campus community and interested in mentoring a diverse array of students consistent with the college's commitment to a Good Neighbor Culture. Duties will include teaching core biology courses to life science majors, an upper-division course in Molecular Biology, and another upper division course within the candidate's area of expertise. In addition to a commitment to high-quality teaching and scholarship, faculty at Berry are expected to involve undergraduates in their research programs, serve as academic advisors, and contribute to the vitality of the residential campus and their professional communities through their service. Requirements: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in biology, molecular biology, or a closely related discipline. Applicants who are ABD should include documentation that the requirements for the degree will be completed by August 2027. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and, accordingly, hires and promotes employees without regard to personal identity characteristics such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit the following: a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position, commitment to the Berry mission, and approach to inclusive teaching and learning; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on October 1 and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Rhodes at drhodes@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204342": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Digital Arts (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Digital Arts (Tenure Track) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Digital Arts (Tenure Track) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Digital Arts (Tenure Track) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Fine Arts Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Sep 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204342 Share Job Description: The Department of Visual and Performing Arts at Berry College seeks a dynamic artist and educator at the assistant professor level (tenure track) to teach digital art in the Art Program. Over the last several years, the Art Program at Berry College has seen an ever-expanding interest in the artistic application of digital technologies from students across the college. The ideal candidate will have expertise in the use of a broad range of digital technologies in the visual arts and their applications across disciplines. This position will support the current digital art curriculum while reimagining what our digital art curriculum could look like. Additionally, we are seeking someone with a strong research practice who is passionate about teaching and mentoring students at a residential liberal arts college. This position will complement and support existing areas in art history, ceramics/ sculpture, and drawing/painting/printmaking. The successful candidate will be committed to supporting the Art Program's mission of creating an environment that promotes creativity and a deep engagement with the creation and history of art. The position starts in August 2027. The successful candidate will join a program that values experimentation, collaboration, and attention to craft while helping students gain hands-on, real-world experiences in the visual arts during their time at Berry. In line with the mission of the college, this position offers opportunities to support student work, community service and engagement, and student research, while promoting access to professional artists. The annual teaching load is 18 hours. Initially, the new faculty will be responsible for teaching existing design courses such as Two-Dimensional Design, Digital Imaging, Graphic Design, and Visual Design for UI, as well as supporting the Studio Art capstone and general education courses. This position carries the expectation of building a new direction for digital art at Berry that is impactful for Art majors/minors, as well as students working across a range of disciplines. This could encompass fields ranging from applied design to animation to new media to social practice. Requirements: Applicants should have earned a terminal degree (MFA or Ph.D.) in a studio art discipline by the date of employment. Further, they should possess classroom experience as an instructor or teaching assistant in digital technologies, while being fluent in course-appropriate applications with the Adobe Creative Cloud. Finally, the successful candidate will share our program's commitment to student engagement inside and outside of the classroom, as well as our interest in promoting opportunities for students. Additional Information: Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and, accordingly, hires and promotes employees without regard to personal identity characteristics such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals with a minimum of 10 examples of student work (pdf); a research statement that discusses how digital applications impact their practice with 20 examples of research (pdf); unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on Monday, October 19, and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Brad Adams, at badams@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204208": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physics (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Physics (Tenure Track) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Physics (Tenure Track) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Physics (Tenure Track) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Physics, Astronomy, and Geology Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204208 Share Job Description: The Department of Physics & Technology at Berry College seeks applicants with a strong interest in teaching undergraduate physics and mentoring undergraduate research in experimental physics. The successful candidate should also be an active participant in the campus community and interested in mentoring and advising students in a residential college environment. The physics program is known for its student-centered teaching methods and mentoring of student research, which has resulted in several Goldwater scholars. With five full-time faculty (including this position), the program awards about 10 physics BS degrees per year and manages a dual-degree engineering program with about 10 transfers per year to partner schools. Facilities include SEM, TEM, XRD, DC magnetron sputtering system, Raman spectrometer, spectrophotometer, spectrofluorometer, 3D printing, and a small observatory. We seek candidates who share our department's commitment to student engagement inside and outside of the classroom, as well as our desire to promote opportunities for students from under-represented groups. Because Berry's undergraduate student population is over 60% female, candidates with strong potential to recruit and mentor women in physics are strongly encouraged to apply. Requirements: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in physics or a closely related field. Applicants who are ABD should include documentation that the requirements for the degree will be completed by August 2027. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and, accordingly, hires and promotes employees without regard to personal identity characteristics such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans involving undergraduates; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Todd Timberlake, at ttimberlake@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204224": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Political Science (Tenure Track) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Political Science (Tenure Track) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Political Science (Tenure Track) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Political Science and International Affairs Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204224 Share Job Description: The Department of Political Science and International Affairs at Berry College seeks a scholar-teacher-mentor who will engage students in courses focusing on campaigns and elections, interest groups, public opinion, or policy (with an American or a regional focus) and is competent to teach social science research methods. We hope to be joined by an innovative teacher who will create new courses that add variety to our curriculum and that invite students from all disciplines into the study of political science and international affairs. This Assistant Professor position begins in August 2027. We are a small, collegial department of scholars committed to excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Our faculty teach across American government, comparative politics, international relations, and political theory, with a shared emphasis on writing, critical thinking, and preparation for meaningful work and advanced study. The Department is further committed to preparing students to become good citizens of the United States and the world. We encourage students to see politics as noble and inspiring. We also encourage students to be politically active no matter what career path they choose to pursue. We are especially interested in candidates whose teaching and scholarship will add variety to the college curriculum and promote our values of respect for and service to others. Mentoring our students as they develop personally and professionally is a high priority. The ideal candidate will contribute to our strategic plan of good citizenship by helping students identify and apply for internships that guide them through experiential learning. The annual teaching load is 18 hours. The successful candidate will typically teach an upper-level course for majors and two sections of a course in our Foundations curriculum (American National Government or Contemporary World Issues) each semester. Faculty are supported with travel funds, work grants, and the opportunity to hire students to support research projects. Requirements: Applicants must hold a PhD in Political Science or a closely related field by August 2027. An active research agenda, an interest in mentoring and guiding undergraduate research, and a demonstrated commitment to teaching undergraduates from a range of disciplines, cultures, and academic backgrounds are essential. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and, accordingly, hires and promotes employees without regard to personal identity characteristics such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on September 30, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Eric C. Sands, at esands@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204321": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sociology (Tenure Track )",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Sociology (Tenure Track ) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Sociology (Tenure Track ) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Sociology (Tenure Track ) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Sociology and Anthropology Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Sep 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204321 Share Job Description: The Sociology and Anthropology Department at Berry College seeks applicants for a tenure-track position in sociology. We seek a sociologist who will bring a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching, mentorship, and research. We especially welcome candidates with experience in applied sociology, community-engaged teaching or research, or other forms of public-facing sociological practice who can contribute to the department's strong commitment to Academic Community Engagement (ACE). This is an open position with preference given to candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: social stratification, health and medicine, social movements, family and the life course, or other areas with strong undergraduate appeal. Applicants should demonstrate how their teaching, service, and scholarship will broaden students' understanding of sociological theory while connecting sociological knowledge to real-world problems, research, professional opportunities, and service. The candidate should also be eager to mentor students pursuing various pathways after graduation, including graduate study and careers involving research, policy, community practice, business, law, teaching, urban and regional planning, health care, and related fields. Berry's foundation in an ethos of service to others makes it a welcoming place for applied, service-oriented, and community-engaged practitioners and scholars. The department has been integral to Academic Community Engagement (ACE) learning at Berry, and we seek a candidate who will develop students' sociological imagination and expand opportunities for hands-on experience in sociology and related academic programs like pre-law, business, and the pre-professional health science program. Berry College has a premier student work program and student scholarship programs that foster strong connections with social service providers, civic organizations, and businesses in the local community. The annual teaching load is 18 hours, typically consisting of three sections of Introduction to Sociology, two electives, and a quantitatively focused course, either the department's required senior capstone course or Introduction to Research Methods. The successful candidate will have opportunities to develop electives reflecting their areas of specialization. Requirements: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in sociology by the date of employment and candidates who are currently ABD should earn their Ph.D. by the date of employment. Additional Information: About Berry College Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities .\" Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors. Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's-level opportunities in business, physician associate studies, and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. College Commitments Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interview or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing their interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values ; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement articulating the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. The review of applications will begin on October 9, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Sarah Allred, Associate Professor of Sociology at sallred@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204329": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Theatre Design (Tenure-Track )",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Theatre Design (Tenure-Track ) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Theatre Design (Tenure-Track ) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Theatre Design (Tenure-Track ) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Fine Arts Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Sep 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204329 Share Job Description: The Department of Visual and Performing Arts at Berry College invites applications for a tenure-track Theatre position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, beginning August 2027. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar and theatre artist with expertise in Scenic and Costume Design and a strong commitment to undergraduate education. We seek a collaborative faculty member who values close interaction with students and contributes to the intellectual, artistic, and residential life of the College. Berry's Theatre program is student-centered and deeply committed to creativity, collaboration, and academic excellence. Through the Berry College Theatre Company (BCTC) , students participate in three mainstage productions annually, gaining hands-on experience in performance and production. Our program emphasizes personalized mentoring, rigorous academic training, and professional development through the LifeWorks student work program. We actively engage artists, students, audiences, and community partners in meaningful dialogue to foster diverse perspectives and inclusive practices. The annual teaching load is 18 hours, typically consisting of a 3-3 load that includes Scenic Design, Costume Design, and related courses, with the possibility of reassigned time for serving as a scenic or costume designer, or supervising student designers for the department's three annual productions. Faculty at Berry receive professional development support and opportunities to collaborate with students on creative and scholarly projects. We especially welcome candidates whose teaching and creative work will enrich the curriculum and reflect Berry's Good Neighbor culture. Requirements: Applicants must hold an MFA in Scenography or a closely related field (Scenic Design or Costume Design) by the date of employment. Additional Information: About Berry College Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities.\" Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors. Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. College Commitments Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interview or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values ; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on October 7th and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Alice Bristow, at abristow@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204248": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Creative Writing - Poetry (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor in Creative Writing - Poetry (Tenure Track) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor in Creative Writing - Poetry (Tenure Track) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant/Associate Professor in Creative Writing - Poetry (Tenure Track) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: English, Rhetoric and Writing Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204248 Share Job Description: The English, Rhetoric, and Writing Department at Berry College seeks a teacher-writer-mentor at the assistant or associate professor level (tenure-track) in poetry writing and writing pedagogy to help meet the needs of our growing creative writing major. We welcome innovative approaches to teaching writing. The department is developing a professional writing minor, and should this be of interest to the hire, they will have the opportunity to develop courses within the minor that align with their interests and expertise. The candidate will be committed to our mission of cultivating astute, creative, and sensitive readers and writers who understand the power and complexity of literature as an artistic expression of human experiences. They will also demonstrate aptitude and enthusiasm for teaching in a liberal arts environment, including teaching first-year writing, and a genuine commitment to mentoring and guiding undergraduate students. The teaching load is 18 hours, which typically translates as 3 courses per semester, and the position starts in August 2027. The successful candidate will be joining a vibrant department housed in the Evans School of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences. The department is collegial, supportive, and committed to the success of our students, providing a range of courses and approaches to literature and creative writing, both traditional and innovative. Faculty at Berry have access to a wide range of professional development opportunities. Our faculty engage with students in and out of the classroom to develop meaningful mentoring relationships such as employing students as research assistants through the college's LifeWorks program, guiding them in undergraduate research, and coaching them in the development of their capstone portfolios. This hire will also assist in bringing in visiting writers for the department's Creative Writing Reading Series, facilitating interactions between our students and a range of successful, published writers. This new faculty member will teach courses in intermediate and advanced poetry and will share responsibilities with the rest of the creative writing faculty in teaching Introduction to Creative Writing, combining study of and instruction in craft with students' creative production. They will also help staff our two unique 400-level courses, Writing about Place and Writing and Community, and will aid us in developing new courses in creative writing. Applicants at the associate professor level may also have the opportunity for leadership roles within the department. The successful candidate should also be an active participant in the campus community and interested in mentoring students consistent with the college's commitment to a Good Neighbor Culture. Requirements: Applicants must hold an MFA or Ph.D. in Creative Writing or a closely related field, and candidates who are currently ABD should earn their Ph.D. by the date of employment. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and, accordingly, hires and promotes employees without regard to personal identity characteristics such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on October 12 and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Clint Peters, at cpeters@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204205": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Mathematics (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor of Mathematics (Tenure Track) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor of Mathematics (Tenure Track) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant/Associate Professor of Mathematics (Tenure Track) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Mathematics and Computer Science Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204205 Share Job Description: The Department of Mathematics and Computer Science at Berry College invites applications for tenure-track assistant/associate professor of mathematics positions to begin in August 2027. We are open to candidates from a variety of mathematical perspectives who want to join a department dedicated to challenging undergraduate students in the classroom. Candidates with teaching interests in abstract algebra, number theory, or geometry; candidates who use computation in their research and teaching; or candidates interested in interdisciplinary collaborations are particularly encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate interest in a residential college environment and enthusiasm for teaching a broad range of mathematics courses at all levels of undergraduate curriculum. The department is dedicated to innovative student-centered pedagogy through active learning methods, growth-focused grading practices, and mentoring students from a wide range of backgrounds. The candidate is expected to establish a strong individual research program that incorporates undergraduate students when appropriate. The candidate should share our department's commitment to student engagement inside and outside of the classroom, as well as our desire to promote opportunities for students from underrepresented groups by participating in existing and developing new student outreach opportunities. Beyond the department, the successful candidate should also be an active participant in the campus community and interested in mentoring a diverse array of students consistent with the college's commitment to a Good Neighbor Culture. Teaching responsibilities included a broad range of courses: core courses in the mathematics and computer science curriculum, electives in the candidate's area(s) of interest, and Foundations (general education) offerings. Tenure-track faculty typically teach 18 credit hours per year, which translates to 5-6 courses per academic year. Support for undergraduate teaching assistants and undergraduate research assistants is available through Berry's LifeWorks program. The candidate will also be supported in applying for Project NExT or other professional development programs. Requirements: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in mathematics, statistics, computer science, or a closely related field. Applicants who are ABD should include documentation that the requirements for the degree will be completed by August 2027. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities . By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and, accordingly, hires and promotes employees without regard to personal identity characteristics such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should visit our employment website (www.berry.edu/employment) to submit the following: a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position, commitment to the Berry mission, and approach to inclusive teaching and learning; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. The review of applications may begin before October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received by October 1, 2026, will receive full consideration. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Garner Cochran, at gcochran@berry.edu. #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204725": {
      "title": "Dean of the Charter School of Education and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Dean of the Charter School of Education and Human Sciences Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Dean of the Charter School of Education and Human Sciences Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Dean of the Charter School of Education and Human Sciences Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Charter School of Education and Human Sciences Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Sep 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204725 Share Job Description: Berry College invites applications and nominations for Dean of the Charter School of Education and Human Sciences . The dean will lead a distinctive multidisciplinary school at an important moment of growth, strengthening established undergraduate and graduate programs, prioritizing engaged student learning, supporting faculty excellence, and helping advance Berry's new strategic plan . As a member of the college's academic leadership team, the dean will shape both the future of the Charter School and contribute to the broader academic direction of the college. The Charter School brings together disciplines devoted to education, health, and behavioral sciences, including the departments of Kinesiology , Psychological Science , Teacher Education , the Division of Nursing (BSN), and the Physician Associate program . The school will launch a master's degree in Athletic Training in 2028. Majors in psychology, exercise science, nursing, and combined education majors have some of the highest enrollments on campus, with growing programs in sport leadership and strategy and minors in applied behavior analysis, family studies, psychology, strength and conditioning, and teaching English as a foreign language. The M.Ed. and Ed.S. programs in teacher education have grown in recent years in partnership with local and regional school systems. The PA program is on track to reach maximum enrollment of the incoming cohort in Fall 2027. The Charter School includes Berry College Elementary and Middle School , a K-8 laboratory school on campus, and two early learning centers, the Child Development Center and the South Rome Early Learning Center . The Charter School boasts a well-established record of community engagement, including internships, certifications, Academic Community Engagement (ACE) courses, and flourishing partnerships with the medical community and other community-based institutions. Students are involved on campus in research and work opportunities that support their academic interests. The dean serves as the chief academic, administrative, and budgetary officer of the Charter School and reports directly to the provost. The dean serves on the Council of School Deans and collaborates with academic affairs leaders. Leadership Priorities Advance the college's strategic plan and mission of educating the head, heart, and hands. Develop a compelling shared vision for the Charter School. Support faculty excellence in teaching, scholarship, professional practice, and mentorship. Nurture clinical, educational, community, and philanthropic partnerships. Discern how to collaboratively and transparently make decisions. Successfully recruit, develop, and retain faculty and staff. Core Responsibilities Supervise all Charter faculty, department chairs, directors, coordinators, and administrative staff. Recommend hiring, reappointment, promotion and tenure, and other personnel actions. Participate in Charter School accreditations, in support of department chairs and directors (ARC-PA, CCNE, Georgia Board of Nursing, Georgia Professional Standards Commission, and CAATE, for the upcoming program in Athletic Training). Assist students and faculty with requests, exceptions, complaints, and the resolution of grievances. Recommend a budget to the provost and oversee the allocation of school funds. Teach one to two courses per academic year, to be worked out in consultation with the provost. Requirements: Earned a doctorate from an accredited institution in one of the Charter School disciplines. A record of teaching, scholarship, and professional accomplishment sufficient for appointment as a tenured full professor in a Charter School department. Significant and progressively responsible academic administrative experience, such as dean, associate dean, director, or department chair, for example. Significant experience with program-level or institutional accreditation. Experience leading in a multidisciplinary academic environment. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and, accordingly, hires and promotes employees without regard to personal identity characteristics such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit A letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values. A curriculum vitae. A statement about the candidate's view of leadership. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Names and contact information of three references. References will not be contacted without prior notice to the candidate. Review of applications will begin October 9, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, candidates should submit materials by that date. The search will be confidential until the finalist stage when on-campus candidate names are shared with Charter School faculty. The anticipated starting date is Summer 2027. Specific questions about the position or nominations may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Alice Suroviec, dean of the School of Mathematical and Natural Sciences, at asuroviec@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205148": {
      "title": "Director of Athletic Training (Graduate Program)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Director of Athletic Training (Graduate Program) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Director of Athletic Training (Graduate Program) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Athletic Training (Graduate Program) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Sep 24, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205148 Share Job Description: Berry College invites applications for its inaugural director of the Master of Science in Athletic Training (MSAT) degree program . The director will be an experienced academic leader who will collaborate with campus partners to plan, coordinate, and complete efforts to establish the Athletic Training graduate program. Among other responsibilities, the director will lead Berry's efforts to earn accreditation from the Commission on Accreditation of Athletic Training Education (CAATE). We seek a dynamic, strategic, and forward-thinking director who can coordinate efforts to deliver a distinctive program. The target date to matriculate the first class is Fall or Summer 2028. Berry College's plans for an Athletic Training degree program are strengthened by a partnership with Atrium Health Floyd, a system of health care providers serving Northwest Georgia and Northeast Alabama. This collaboration reflects a shared commitment to strengthening the health care workforce by creating mentored pathways from graduate education to professional practice, benefiting students while addressing workforce needs and serving the communities we jointly support. This partnership, along with a strong internal collaboration with Berry College Athletics, positions the inaugural director to develop an exceptional program. The ideal candidate will bring a strong background of academic and clinical experience with creative and innovative approaches for developing a regionally competitive AT program. The director's faculty appointment will be commensurate with his or her experience. Candidates with the appropriate credentials will be considered for tenure at the time of appointment. The director will collaborate with other AT faculty to ensure effective organization, administration, fiscal management, educational goals/assessment/analysis, clinical site establishment, and oversight of the didactic and clinical curriculum. In recent years, Berry College has launched a physician associate program and has expanded its BSN nursing program, both located in the newly opened Morgan Bailey Hall for Health Sciences. The Exercise Science major is one of the college's top undergraduate majors and will complement this new program in close partnership. Additionally, the Cage Athletic Center will be a significant resource for the program. Rome, Georgia, is home to a robust network of hospitals, specialty clinics, and regional medical centers, creating an exceptional environment for experiential learning and clinical education. The combination of Berry's academic excellence, dynamic athletic programs, and Rome's thriving health care landscape provides students with exposure to professional practice, meaningful community engagement, and a strong foundation for health-related careers. Requirements: An earned doctoral degree in a relevant field Contemporary expertise in Athletic Training Certification and good standing with the Board of Certification NPI number with appropriate health care field designation Eligible for Georgia state credentialing and in good standing with the state regulatory agency in Georgia Previous clinical practice as an athletic trainer Previous full-time academic appointment with teaching responsibilities 3 years of experience in post-secondary education, preferably as director, associate director, or clinical coordinator Preferred experience with AT curriculum development and implementation Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business, physician associate studies, and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interview or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Candidates must submit: 1. A letter expressing qualifications and interest in the position 2. A curriculum vitae 3. Undergraduate and graduate transcripts 4. Statements of teaching and leadership philosophy 5. Names and contact information for three references The review of applications will begin October 19 and continue until a suitable candidate is identified. Specific questions may be sent directly to the search committee chair, Associate Provost Dr.  Alan Hughes, at rhughes@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205002": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Entrepreneurship (Two-Year Appointment)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor of Entrepreneurship (Two-Year Appointment) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor of Entrepreneurship (Two-Year Appointment) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Visiting Assistant Professor of Entrepreneurship (Two-Year Appointment) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: CSOB Locations: Mt Berry, GA Posted: Sep 18, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205002 Share Job Description: The AACSB-accredited Campbell School of Business at Berry College invites applications for a two-year Visiting Assistant Professor of Entrepreneurship beginning August 2027. Rooted in Berry's mission of educating the head, heart, and hands, we seek a teacher-mentor-scholar who is passionate about helping students identify opportunities, launch new ventures, and grow organizations. The ideal candidate will be committed to supporting students as they transform ideas into successful enterprises and prepare to lead with integrity and purpose. The Campbell School is known for its close-knit community of faculty, staff, and students, its emphasis on experiential learning, and its integration of business education with Berry's broader mission. Entrepreneurship has long been a distinctive strength of the School, and this position offers exceptional opportunities to work closely with students through mentoring, applied projects, competitions, and venture development activities in partnership with our Center for Student Entrepreneurship Education and Development (C-SEED) . Berry's entrepreneurship ecosystem includes resources that support student venture creation, mentorship, experiential learning, and leadership. Teaching responsibilities include undergraduate and MBA entrepreneurship and management courses, with a standard teaching load of 21 credit hours (typically seven courses) per year. The successful candidate should demonstrate enthusiasm for mentoring students and connecting them with entrepreneurs, executives, alumni, and community leaders who can serve as mentors, speakers, and collaborators. Candidates with academic or professional experience in entrepreneurship, innovation, new venture creation, small business leadership, or related fields are especially encouraged to apply. Requirements: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. or DBA in Entrepreneurship, Management, Strategy, or a related field, and candidates who are currently ABD should earn their doctoral degree by the date of employment. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities . Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interview or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values (linked above); a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on October 15 and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Eric Kushins, at ekushins@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204565": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of French",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor of French Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor of French Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Visiting Assistant Professor of French Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Foreign Languages Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Sep 8, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204565 Share Job Description: The Department of World Languages and Cultures at Berry College invites applications for a visiting assistant professor of French to begin in August 2027. The ideal candidate will have experience and enthusiasm for teaching lower- and intermediate-level courses in the college setting as well as an ability to teach upper-level courses in literature, French cinema and culture, and/or linguistics, etc. This is a two-year visiting appointment with the possibility of extending to a third year. The department is committed to providing students with the opportunity of becoming proficient in the languages, literatures and cultures of the languages it offers, and to gain cross- and intercultural competency and global awareness. It seeks to graduate majors and minors with advanced communicative skills in speaking, listening, reading, and writing, cultural knowledge of other countries, and a sophisticated understanding of the problems and promises that a globalized world presents. The department also boasts graduates who have won numerous prestigious fellowships, such as the Fulbright and the Critical Language Scholarship. Requirements: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in French or a closely related field, and candidates who are currently ABD should earn their Ph.D. by the date of employment. Additional Information: About Berry College Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities.\" Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors. Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. College Commitments Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interview or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values (linked above); a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on October 15 and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Vincent Gregoire, at vgregoire@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204250": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor or Visiting Lecturer of Speech",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor or Visiting Lecturer of Speech Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor or Visiting Lecturer of Speech Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Visiting Assistant Professor or Visiting Lecturer of Speech Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Communication Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204250 Share Job Description: The Communication Department at Berry College seeks a Visiting Lecturer or Visiting Assistant Professor of Speech. We seek a faculty member who is committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching and has expertise in public speaking and rhetoric. Public speaking is one of three required courses for all students at Berry and is at the core of our departmental mission to graduate effective, persuasive, and ethical communicators. The visiting position is renewable annually for up to three years. Berry's Communication program is one of the largest majors at the college and comprises five concentrations: Communication and Media Studies, Digital and Social Media, Filmmaking and Cinematic Arts, Public Relations, and Sports Communication. We are a vibrant, collegial department focused on preparing students for the media industry and/or graduate studies. Our students create content inside and outside the classroom, working with co-curricular student organizations, including the Berry College Forensics Union and five student-run media divisions. Berry students regularly win national awards for their excellence in public speaking and media content. This position will primarily deliver course sections of public speaking to students from across the college. Our public speaking course emphasizes persuasion, storytelling, visual competency, and students engaging topics of public importance through personal experience. Faculty may design sections of public speaking around special topics of student interest. Past examples include leadership, healthcare, social justice, and political communication. There is also the opportunity to teach an occasional upper-division section aligned with the candidate's expertise, such as communication theory, human communication, and interpersonal communication. We are especially interested in candidates seeking a liberal arts approach to higher education. Requirements: Candidates must have experience teaching college-level public speaking. Candidates must have a Master's Degree in Communication, Rhetoric, or Speech to be appointed as a Visiting Lecturer. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Communication, Speech, Rhetoric, or a closely related field at the time of employment to be appointed as a Visiting Assistant Professor. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and, accordingly, hires and promotes employees without regard to personal identity characteristics such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; a statement of research plans; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on October 19, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Curt Hersey, at chersey@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203526": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Athletic Trainer Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Athletic Trainer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Athletic Trainer Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203526 Share Job Description: Berry College invites applications and nominations for the full-time, 10-month position of assistant athletic trainer. RESPONSIBILITIES : Reporting to the Head Athletic Trainer. The assistant athletic trainer will be responsible for assisting with sport coverage, administrative duties, supervision of student workers, and compliance with the NCAA Division III sports medicine policies and procedures. An integral part of the position is mentoring student workers and implementation of educational programs within the sports medicine department. General duties include, but are not limited to: preventing, treating, and rehabilitating athletic injuries; managing daily operations; assisting with inventory and budget; assisting with assigned teams insurance claims; traveling with assigned team when necessary; acting as a liaison between the student-athlete and his/her coach, team physician(s), and parents; and performing other duties assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer. Requirements: Master's degree required. The candidate should possess good communication skills, strong leadership and mentoring abilities, and the ability to create a culture that is both disciplined and caring. Effective and efficient organizational skills and the ability to work unsupervised are required. Candidate must be Advanced Level CPR Certified through the American Red Cross or American Heart Association. He/she must also be NATABOC certified and Georgia State Licensed or eligible. The successful candidate must also be able to work non-traditional hours including nights, weekends, and holidays. The candidate will also demonstrate an understanding of and commitment to a liberal arts education, Division III athletics, and an appreciation for and commitment to all NCAA , Southern Athletic Association (SAA ), and institutional rules and regulations. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application, resume, and the contact information for three professional references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until a qualified individual has been hired. No phone calls or e-mails, please. Berry College is an equal opportunity employer. For ADA Accommodations, please reach out to our ADA Coordinator at VTTY 706-233-4062. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203265": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's & Women's Tennis Coach",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Men's & Women's Tennis Coach Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Men's & Women's Tennis Coach Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Men's & Women's Tennis Coach Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 3, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203265 Share Job Description: Berry College invites applications and nominations for the full-time, 10-month position of assistant men's & women's tennis coach, with additional responsibilities to be assigned based on the successful candidates' skill sets and experience. Berry challenges students to embrace a firsthand educational experience that complements challenging academic programs with opportunities for meaningful student work experiences, spiritual and moral growth, and significant service to others.   This is a unique opportunity to be part of a program grounded in the college's mission and incorporating an integrated education of the head, the heart, and the hands. RESPONSIBILITIES: Reporting to the Head Men's & Women's Tennis Coach, the successful candidate will be responsible for assisting the Head Coach with the organization, supervision, and administration of an NCAA Division III intercollegiate tennis program.  The candidate will also demonstrate an understanding of and commitment to a liberal arts education, Division III athletics, and an appreciation for and commitment to all NCAA, Southern Athletic Association (SAA), and institutional rules and regulations.  The candidates should also possess good communication skills, strong leadership and mentoring abilities, and the ability to create a culture that is both disciplined and caring.  Other duties and responsibilities may include, but are not limited to, recruitment of academically and athletically qualified student-athletes, budget management, practice and game preparation/management, scheduling, compliance, public relations, alumni communication, student work supervision, fundraising, equipment management, and a commitment to the student-athlete's academic progress and degree completion.  Along with coaching responsibilities, the candidates will be assigned additional responsibilities dependent on the successful candidates' skill set and experiences. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required, Master's degree preferred.  Previous coaching and/or playing experience at the collegiate level is preferred.  This position includes competitive benefits and a salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities . By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodation are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application, resume, and the contact information for three professional references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until a qualified individual has been hired. No phone calls or e-mails, please. Berry College is an equal opportunity employer. For ADA Accommodations, please reach out to our ADA Coordinator at VTTY 706-233-4062. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205631": {
      "title": "Assistant Teacher, Full-Time",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Assistant Teacher, Full-Time Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Teacher, Full-Time Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Teacher, Full-Time Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Charter School of Education and Human Sciences Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Oct 8, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205631 Share Job Description: The Charter School of Education and Human Sciences at Berry College invites applications for a Full-Time Assistant Teacher at the Berry College Child Development Center (CDC). We are seeking an enthusiastic, compassionate, patient, and dedicated early childhood educator who is committed to creating a safe, inclusive, nurturing, and developmentally appropriate learning environment for young children. The Berry College Child Development Cente r is a private, tuition-based laboratory school operated under the governance of Berry College's Charter School of Education and Human Sciences . Licensed by the Georgia Department of Early Care and Learning (DECAL) , the CDC provides a high-quality early childhood education experience for children ages three through five. The Center serves as a model learning environment that integrates the resources of Berry College with research-based best practices in early childhood education. Position Responsibilities The Assistant Teacher works collaboratively with the Lead Teacher to support all aspects of the preschool classroom. Responsibilities include: Assisting with daily classroom instruction, activities, and routines. Supporting lesson planning, preparation, organization, and implementation of developmentally appropriate learning experiences. Facilitating small-group and individualized learning activities. Supervising children during instructional activities, free-choice play, outdoor experiences, meals, transitions, and other classroom routines. Creating and maintaining a positive, welcoming, and inclusive classroom environment. Supporting children's social-emotional, cognitive, physical, and language development. Maintaining accurate records and documentation required by state licensing regulations. Communicating professionally and effectively with children, families, colleagues, and Berry College students. Maintaining confidentiality regarding children, families, and Center operations. Assisting with the training, guidance, and supervision of student workers. Collaborating with the Lead Teacher and CDC staff to ensure consistent classroom practices and high-quality care. Participating in professional development and contributing to the continued improvement of the Center's educational program. The position is full-time, 40 hours per week, 12 months per year (July-June) and includes a comprehensive benefits package. Berry College provides eligible employees with a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, disability, and life insurance, as well as education and retirement benefits. Additional information regarding employee benefits is available through Berry College Human Resources . The ideal candidate will enjoy working with children ages four and five, demonstrate an understanding of early childhood development and learning, and be committed to providing each child with a supportive, engaging, and enriching educational experience. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Associate degree in early childhood education, elementary education, child development, or a related field. Training or coursework in early childhood education, elementary education, child development, or a related field. At least two years of professional experience working with young children in an early childhood education setting. Strong interpersonal, communication, organizational, and classroom-management skills. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in early childhood education, elementary education, child development, or a related field. Three or more years of experience working in an early childhood education setting. Experience working with preschool-aged children in a licensed early childhood program. Knowledge of developmentally appropriate practices and early childhood learning standards. Experience supporting inclusive classrooms and children with diverse learning and developmental needs. Additional Information: About Berry College Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business, physician associate studies, teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. The college provides medical, dental, disability, and life insurance, benefits at no cost to employees and at reduced rates for a spouse and dependents. Education and retirement benefits are also available to employees, spouses, and dependents after one year of employment. College Commitments Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interview or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a complete application that includes: A cover letter A resume Copies of all transcripts Names and contact information for three references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. The anticipated start date for the position is November 2, 2026, or as mutually agreed upon. Final candidates will be required to successfully complete a comprehensive background check in accordance with Berry College and applicable state requirements. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=140220": {
      "title": "Berry College Laboratory Schools - Substitute Teachers.",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Berry College Laboratory Schools - Substitute Teachers. Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Berry College Laboratory Schools - Substitute Teachers. Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Berry College Laboratory Schools - Substitute Teachers. Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Edu & Hu Sci Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Dec 6, 2021 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Position ID: 140220 Share Job Description: These positions are located at Berry College Elementary and Middle School (BCEMS), the Child Development Center (CDC), or the South Rome Early Learning Center (SRELC). The Berry College laboratory schools (BCEMS, CDC, and SRELC) are private, tuition-based schools under the governance of the Berry College Charter School of Education and Human Sciences. Berry's laboratory schools combine the remarkable resources of Berry College with talented faculty and staff to provide an outstanding example of best practices for education. Berry's CDC and SRELC offer preschool educational programs (SRELC is only for 3-year-olds); Berry's BCEMS serves K-8. Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Applicants for this position should have a high school diploma, but a bachelor's degree is preferred. Previous experience working in educational settings or having served as a substitute is a plus. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodations are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a complete application that includes: a cover letter, resume, copies of transcripts (if applicable), and the names of three references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Persons applying for employment with Berry College will be required to submit a full background check. Berry College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty and staff. We are particularly interested in receiving applications from members of underrepresented groups. Website: https://www.berry.edu/srelc/ START DATE: As needed Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=136365": {
      "title": "Campus Police Officer.",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Campus Police Officer. Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Campus Police Officer. Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Campus Police Officer. Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Campus Police Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Sep 7, 2021 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Hourly Position ID: 136365 Share Job Description: Berry College Police Department seeks applications for the full-time position of Police Officer. Berry College Police Officers are P.O.S.T. certified officers who provide 24 hour a day seven day a week law enforcement/security services to the college. Located midway between Atlanta, Ga., and Chattanooga, Tenn., on a 27,000-acre campus just north of Rome, Ga., Berry College is an independent, coeducational, liberal arts college with approximately 2,100 undergraduate and graduate students. Berry College challenges students to embrace a firsthand educational experience that connects challenging academic programs with opportunities for meaningful student work experiences, spiritual and moral growth, and significant service to others. Berry College is proud of its history of liberal arts blended with professional programs, and its enduring commitment to Christian values and integrated education of the head, the heart, and the hands. Duties include: Patrol the college campus in an effort to prevent, deter and discover any personal or property crimes Respond to emergency situations Perform security checks Investigate traffic accidents and report crimes Enforce traffic and parking regulations Enforce federal, state, local laws and college regulations as applicable Preparation of accurate and timely law enforcement related records and reports The Police Officer position at Berry College includes working days, nights, weekend shifts, and holidays as assigned. Requirements: Georgia P.O.S.T. Certification as a Police Officer At least 21 years old Good verbal and written communication skills Previous experience with a full service agency preferred Some college course work or credit preferred Must meet all P.O.S.T. requirements annually to stay certified Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodations are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit an online application, cover letter, resume, and information for three professional references. Review of candidates will begin immediately and will continue until position is filled. Berry College is an equal opportunity employer. For ADA Accommodations please contact our ADA Coordinator VTTY 706-233-4062. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=170986": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper.",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Groundskeeper. Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Groundskeeper. Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Groundskeeper. Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Physical Plant Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Dec 15, 2023 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 170986 Share Job Description: 1.   Responsible for maintaining the college landscaping and grounds, minor repair to grounds equipment, and other grounds keeping tasks to maintain a safe and attractive environment. 2.  Examines the college grounds on a routine basis, weeds flower beds, and mulch around shrubs, trees, buildings and natural areas. 3.  Maintains streets and parking lots in the immediate vicinity of the main campus by vacuuming curbs, cleaning street drains, and unstopping drains with the sewage machine as directed. 4.  Moves dead branches and trees, prunes and maintains trees. Inspects trees for damage from pests and disease. Grinds stumps and saves mulch for future use. 5.  Supervise and train student workers on equipment and safety procedures within specific zone. Requirements: 1.  Able to safely operate various grounds equipment 2. Understand the proper uses of safety equipment in accordance with OSHA standards and procedures 3. Keeping Beautification of Berry College grounds 4. Oversee student workers; arrange schedules; delegate tasks Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodations are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a application, and the contact information for three professional references. The job is open until filled. Application review will begin immediately. Berry College is an equal opportunity employer. Anyone applying for employment with Berry College will submit to a national background check Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=155762": {
      "title": "Housekeeper.",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Housekeeper. Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Housekeeper. Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Housekeeper. Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Physical Plant Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Nov 11, 2022 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 155762 Share Job Description: Clean floor areas by sweeping, vacuuming, mopping, stripping, buffing, or waxing; clean work areas by washing, wiping, and/or dusting furniture, windows, and related equipment. Maintain bathroom areas by cleaning toilets, sinks, floors, and tubs/showers; refill toilet paper, paper towels, and soap in dispensers as needed. Empty and/or dispose of trash/recycling. Maintain equipment, supplies, storage areas, records, student timesheets, and operation reports. Supervise student workers and perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: Operating equipment sweeping, mopping, dusting, vacuuming, buffing, waxing Cleaning bathrooms and other assigned areas Correct usage of equipment and chemicals Basic computer skills for campus communications, H.R. testing Supervising student workers, communicating with coworkers and other campus employees Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring that facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodations are welcome. You can reach out to us at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a application, and the contact information for three professional references. The job is open until filled. Application review will begin immediately. Berry College is an equal opportunity employer. Anyone applying for employment with Berry College will submit to a national background check. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
