    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203735": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant to the President",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Senior Executive Assistant to the President Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Senior Executive Assistant to the President Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Executive Assistant to the President Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: President's Office Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Aug 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203735 Share Job Description: The Executive Assistant to the President provides comprehensive executive-level administrative support to the President and serves as the primary coordinator of the President's Office. The Senior Executive Assistant manages the President's schedule, communications, travel, budget administration, and office operations while exercising confidentiality, independent judgment, discretion, and professionalism in support of the President's priorities and activities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Executive Administration Manage the President's calendar, appointments, meetings, speaking and community engagements. Coordinate requests for the President's time and establish meeting priorities. Arrange travel and prepare itineraries for the President. Prepare and process expense reports and related documentation. Board of Trustees, Executive Leadership Team and Cabinet Assist members of the Board of Trustees by answering questions, directing them to the appropriate administrator, and scheduling Executive Committee meetings. Attend all board meetings and prepare and distribute board agendas, materials, and supporting documentation. Assist with three board of trustees meetings and management of OnBoard (board of trustees software platform). Responsible for taking board minutes and drafting other board-related materials including agendas, resolutions, and letters of appreciation. Supporting both the Executive Leadership Team and Cabinet in developing agendas, collecting documentation, taking minutes, posting agendas, and acting as event coordinator for meetings and retreats. Communications and Correspondence Draft, edit, and coordinate presidential correspondence, reports, presentations, and communications. Manage incoming and outgoing communications on behalf of the President. Review materials prepared for the President's signature to ensure quality, completeness, and accuracy. Serve as a liaison between the President's Office and internal and external constituents. Research and Special Projects Conduct research and prepare briefing materials, reports, and background information as requested by the President. Support presidential initiatives and special projects. Develop and implement systems that increase efficiency within the President's Office. Office Administration and Budget Oversee daily administrative operations of the President's Office. Maintain office files, records, and correspondence. Manage receipts, p-card reconciliations and approvals, memberships, subscriptions, invoices, and reimbursements. Welcome and assist visitors to the President's Office. Other Duties Contributes to the overall success of the College by undertaking special projects and other essential duties and responsibilities as assigned by the President. Requirements: High school diploma required; an associate or bachelor's degree preferred Three to seven years of dedicated experience supporting C-suite or senior executives Advanced computer literacy: Microsoft Office Suite, cloud systems, and virtual meeting tools Discretion: Proven capacity to maintain absolute confidentiality Communication: Exceptional written and verbal communication skills Problem-solving: Strong independent decision-making and project coordination Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business, physician associate studies, and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit an application, cover letter, resume, and information for three professional references. Review of candidates will begin immediately. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203949": {
      "title": "TRIO Student Support Services (SSS) Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: TRIO Student Support Services (SSS) Program Coordinator Berry College \n\tJob Posting: TRIO Student Support Services (SSS) Program Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details TRIO Student Support Services (SSS) Program Coordinator Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Services Locations: Mt Berry, GA Posted: Aug 20, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 203949 Share Job Description: Berry College invites applications for the position of Program Coordinator for TRIO Student Support Services (SSS) . TRIO Student Support Services is a federally funded program that supports first-generation college students, students from limited-income households, and students with documented disabilities as they persist toward graduation and successful post-baccalaureate outcomes. Reporting to the Director of TRIO Student Support Services, the Coordinator serves as a student-facing professional who provides individualized support, develops and implements student success programming, tracks participant outcomes, and contributes to the achievement of federal grant objectives. The Coordinator works collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and community partners to promote academic success, personal development, leadership, financial well-being, and career readiness. RESPONSIBILITES: Provide individualized success coaching, academic support, and resource referrals to TRIO SSS participants. Recruit, identify, and enroll eligible students in accordance with federal grant requirements. Manage an assigned caseload of approximately 120 TRIO SSS participants, providing proactive outreach, individualized support, progress monitoring, and intervention strategies designed to promote persistence, academic achievement, and timely degree completion. Monitor student academic progress and implement retention and intervention strategies that support student success. Plan and facilitate workshops, educational events, and enrichment activities related to academic achievement, financial literacy, health and wellness, leadership development, graduate school preparation, career readiness, and student engagement. Track student participation, maintain participant records, and ensure accurate documentation of services delivered. Assist with collection, analysis, and reporting of program data to support assessment efforts and federal reporting requirements. Supervise and mentor TRIO student leaders, peer mentors, and/or LifeWorks student employees. Collaborate with faculty and campus partners to connect students with academic support and campus resources. Assist with implementation of educational, and community-building experiences that support the holistic development of participants. Support the Director in ensuring compliance with U.S. Department of Education regulations and achievement of grant objectives. Represent TRIO Student Support Services at campus events, recruiting activities, and institutional initiatives related to student success. WORK ENVIRONMENT: This position is well-suited for a candidate who enjoys meaningful engagement with students, collaborative partnerships across campus, and hands-on program leadership within a mission-driven college environment. Successful candidates will demonstrate a genuine commitment to student development, educational opportunity, and helping students overcome barriers to success. The Coordinator is expected to maintain meaningful relationships with an assigned caseload of approximately 120 participants and contribute directly to the program's federally established objectives related to retention, academic success, graduation, and post-baccalaureate enrollment. This position is funded through the federally supported TRIO Student Support Services grant. Berry College is currently operating in the fifth and final year of its 2022-2027 grant cycle and has received notification of continued funding for the 2027-2032 grant period. Continued employment remains contingent upon the availability of federal grant funding and successful grant renewal outcomes. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required; master's degree in higher education, counseling, student affairs, social work, education, or a related field preferred. Experience working with college students in advising, coaching, mentoring, educational opportunity programs, or related student-support roles. Demonstrated commitment to supporting first-generation students, students from limited-income backgrounds, students with disabilities, and other underserved student populations. Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.? Demonstrated ability to build relationships with students and work effectively with campus and community constituencies. Ability to maintain confidential student information and exercise sound professional judgment. Ability to work occasional evening and weekend hours in support of program activities. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities . By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for the quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate- and master's-level opportunities in business, physician associate studies, and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit an online application, cover letter, resume, and information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Director of TRIO Student Support Services, Cecelia Raja, craja@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205711": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Marketing (Two-Year Appointment)",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor of Marketing (Two-Year Appointment) Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor of Marketing (Two-Year Appointment) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Visiting Assistant Professor of Marketing (Two-Year Appointment) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: CSOB Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Oct 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205711 Share Job Description: The AACSB-accredited Campbell School of Business at Berry College invites applications for a two-year Visiting Assistant Professor of Marketing beginning August 2027. Rooted in Berry's mission of educating the head, heart, and hands , we seek a teacher-mentor-scholar who will help students apply marketing concepts and develop the knowledge, skills, and professional perspective to succeed and lead with integrity and purpose. Candidates with academic or professional experience in marketing analytics, digital marketing, marketing communication, or related fields are especially encouraged to apply. The Campbell School is known for its close-knit community, emphasis on experiential learning, and integration of business education with Berry's broader mission. As a vital part of the curriculum, marketing offers opportunities for faculty to engage students in applied projects and professional development that strengthen leadership, communication, and analytical skills. Teaching responsibilities include undergraduate marketing courses such as Principles of Marketing , as well as possible courses in business statistics, business communication, or the MBA program, depending on the candidate's qualifications and experience. The standard teaching load is 21 credit hours, typically seven courses, per year. There are also opportunities to teach undergraduate marketing electives aligned with the candidate's area of expertise. The successful candidate should demonstrate enthusiasm for mentoring students and creating meaningful learning experiences that integrate marketing theory with applied business practice. Requirements: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. or DBA in Marketing or a related field, and candidates who are currently ABD should earn their doctoral degree by the date of employment. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \"We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interview or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit a letter of application describing the candidate's interest in this position and commitment to the Berry mission and values ; a curriculum vitae; a teaching statement that should articulate the candidate's teaching approach, experience, and goals; complete teaching evaluations; unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts; and names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on November 2 and will continue until the position is filled. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Anna Vredeveld, at avredeveld@berry.edu #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205716": {
      "title": "Berry Center for Integrity in Leadership Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Berry Center for Integrity in Leadership Operations Coordinator Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Berry Center for Integrity in Leadership Operations Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Berry Center for Integrity in Leadership Operations Coordinator Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Affairs Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Oct 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205716 Share Job Description: The Operations Coordinator provides the operational infrastructure that enables the Berry Center for Integrity in Leadership (BCIL) to carry out its partnerships, grants, convenings, programs, and institutional initiatives reliably and effectively. Reporting to the Sims Director, the Coordinator works across the BCIL team and with campus and external partners to translate approved priorities into well-organized plans, schedules, logistics, communications, financial processes, and follow-through. This position is well suited for a collaborative, self-directed professional who enjoys coordinating complex work, improving operating systems, working with students and partners, and helping programs move successfully from planning through implementation and closeout. Key Responsibilities Coordinate the operational implementation of BCIL partnerships, grants, convenings, programs, institutional initiatives, and special projects, including timelines, schedules, responsibilities, resources, and follow-through. Contribute actively to BCIL's professional team by bringing initiative, sound judgment, and ideas to team planning, problem solving, and continuous improvement; help strengthen the Center's operating practices, participant experience, and overall effectiveness. Participate directly in BCIL initiatives and, as assigned, support, co-facilitate, or lead selected program components under the direction of the appropriate professional lead, providing opportunities for increasing contribution as experience and capability develop. Coordinate lectures, workshops, retreats, mentoring activities, student programs, faculty and staff development programs, and other events, including registration, facilities, catering, travel, accommodations, audiovisual needs, materials, and participant communication. Maintain project plans, calendars, status trackers, records, workflows, templates, and other operating systems that support reliable execution across multiple concurrent initiatives. Administer purchasing, invoices, reimbursements, travel expenses, contracts, purchase-card activity, and budget-tracking processes in accordance with College policies and approved budgets. Support assessment, grant reporting, donor stewardship, annual reporting, and program review by maintaining accurate participation, financial, and activity records. Work Environment The Operations Coordinator works within a small, collaborative professional team and routinely coordinates work across organizational boundaries. The position requires a high degree of organization, professional judgment, follow-through, and attention to detail. Occasional evening or weekend work is required in support of programs and events. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required; minimum of three years of progressively responsible experience in program operations, project coordination, event or program administration, or comparable operational work. Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple projects, programs, or events involving schedules, deadlines, participants, resources, and multiple stakeholders. Strong organizational, project-management, communication, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to manage concurrent responsibilities and changing priorities. Experience supporting budgets, purchasing, reimbursements, financial records, or comparable administrative processes. Demonstrated ability to work effectively and professionally with students, faculty, staff, institutional leaders, external partners, vendors, and community members. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. Combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experiences and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate and master's level opportunities in business, physician associate studies, and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit an online application, cover letter, resume, and information for three professional references. Review of candidates will begin November 9, 2026, with priority given to applications received by November 8, 2026. Specific questions about the position may be sent directly to Berry College Human Resources at employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    },
    "https://berry.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206082": {
      "title": "Bonner Scholars Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Berry College\nJob Posting: Bonner Scholars Program Coordinator Berry College \n\tJob Posting: Bonner Scholars Program Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Bonner Scholars Program Coordinator Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Services Locations: Mount Berry, GA Posted: Oct 22, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 206082 Share Job Description: Berry College invites applications for the position of Bonner Scholars Program Coordinator. The Bonner Scholars Program is a nationally recognized scholarship and leadership development program that prepares students for lives of service, civic engagement, and social responsibility through sustained community engagement, leadership education, and experiential learning. Reporting to the Director of Community Engagement, the Coordinator provides leadership for the day-to-day administration of the Bonner Scholars Program and works closely with students, campus partners, community organizations, alumni, and the Bonner Foundation to advance the program's mission. The Coordinator serves as a student-facing professional who mentors scholars, coordinates developmental programming, maintains program records, cultivates community partnerships, and helps students connect service experiences with their academic, personal, and professional growth. RESPONSIBILITIES: Coordinate the daily operations of the Bonner Scholars Program and support implementation of the program's developmental model, expectations, and annual calendar. Assist with the recruitment, selection, onboarding, and orientation of Bonner Scholars in collaboration with campus partners. Advise and mentor Bonner Scholars throughout their collegiate experience, providing proactive outreach, individualized support, progress monitoring, and referrals to campus resources. Plan and facilitate orientation, leadership development, reflection, enrichment, community-building, and educational programming for Bonner Scholars. Support students in connecting community engagement experiences with academic learning, career preparation, leadership development, and personal growth. Supervise and mentor student leaders and/or LifeWorks student employees associated with the Bonner Scholars Program. Cultivate and maintain collaborative relationships with nonprofit organizations, schools, agencies, and other community partners. Identify meaningful community engagement placements and work with partners to promote mutually beneficial, well-supported student experiences. Monitor scholar participation and progress; maintain accurate student records, service-hour documentation, and other program records. Assist with collection, analysis, and reporting of program data to support assessment, institutional reporting, and Bonner Foundation expectations. Assist with budget management, event planning, communications, travel, and program logistics. Collaborate with colleagues across Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, and other campus areas to support scholar success and community engagement. Represent the Bonner Scholars Program at campus events, community meetings, and regional or national Bonner gatherings. Contribute to institutional initiatives that advance student success, leadership development, belonging, civic responsibility, and Berry's Good Neighbor Culture. WORK ENVIRONMENT: This position is well-suited for a candidate who enjoys meaningful engagement with students, collaborative partnerships across campus and in the community, and hands-on program leadership within a mission-driven college environment. Successful candidates will demonstrate a genuine commitment to mentoring students, strengthening community partnerships, and helping scholars develop as thoughtful leaders and engaged citizens. The Coordinator is expected to maintain meaningful relationships with Bonner Scholars, contribute to a strong cohort experience, and support consistent fulfillment of program expectations. The role involves regular coordination with community partners and campus colleagues, along with periodic evening, weekend, and travel commitments connected to retreats, service activities, conferences, and special events. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required; master's degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, social work, nonprofit leadership, public administration, education, or a related field preferred. Experience working with college students, leadership programs, community engagement initiatives, service-learning programs, nonprofit organizations, or related settings. Familiarity with the Bonner Program model and/or demonstrated success working with students from diverse economic and educational backgrounds. Commitment to student development, educational opportunity, civic engagement, and mutually beneficial community partnerships. Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple priorities, detailed records, events, and program timelines. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to maintain confidential student information and exercise sound professional judgment. Ability to work occasional evening and weekend hours and travel in support of program activities. Experience with program assessment, reporting, event planning, budget management, or scholarship-program administration preferred. Additional Information: ABOUT BERRY COLLEGE Berry is a selective independent college of 2,200 students located adjacent to Rome, GA, midway between Atlanta, GA, and Chattanooga, TN. Berry's educational approach deliberately unites challenging academic programs with practical work experience in a residential campus community that encourages faith and emphasizes caring for the needs of others above self. Our mission and values are grounded in the ethic that our founder instilled more than a century ago: \" We educate the head, heart, and hands - to inspire leaders of integrity who cultivate thriving communities. By combining academic exploration with meaningful work responsibilities in a residential setting, our approach emphasizes firsthand experience and mentoring. We invest in the personal growth and professional preparation of talented students from varied backgrounds, with an enduring commitment to help those hindered by financial need. Guided by Christian principles, we value the dignity of individuals, the search for truth tempered with grace, and the well-being of our neighbors.\" Nationally recognized for the quality of learning and quality of life, Berry offers first-rate undergraduate degree programs in the sciences, humanities, arts, and human sciences, as well as undergraduate- and master's-level opportunities in business, physician associate studies, and teacher education. The College's stunning 27,000-acre campus affords opportunities that cannot be duplicated elsewhere. Berry's ongoing commitment is to provide exceptional educational experiences to talented students from a wide range of social, racial, and economic backgrounds. COLLEGE COMMITMENTS Berry College is committed to recruiting and supporting a diverse faculty and staff. An Equal Opportunity Institution, Berry complies with all applicable laws and provisions prohibiting discrimination in its educational and employment policies. Berry respects the essential dignity of all individuals and accordingly hires and promotes employees without regard to matters of personal identity such as race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, and political affiliation. Berry College is committed to ensuring facilities, programs, services, and activities are accessible to everyone, including those seeking employment at Berry College. Inquiries about interviews or workplace accommodations are welcomed and can be directed to employment@berry.edu or (706) 233-4062. Application Instructions: Applicants should submit an online application, cover letter, resume, and information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Director of Community Engagement, Devon Smyth, at dsmyth@berry.edu . #HEJ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Berry College 2277 Martha Berry Hwy NW Mount Berry, GA 30149"
    }
  },
